{"repositoryId":1313853269,"availability":"available","full":"iamrohithrnair/emeraldian","name":"emeraldian","description":"A terminal UI for your Obsidian vault: live-preview notes, backlinks, images, a force-directed graph and an assistant","category":"Productivity","language":"Rust","stars":532,"forks":20,"created":"2026-07-27T13:04:41Z","updated":"2026-09-26T19:02:52Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://emeraldian-tui.github.io","topics":[],"demo":"https://emeraldian-tui.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.710Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.710Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.710Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.710Z","stars":532,"forks":20}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The best TUI for Obsidian. Your vault, the way you already know it: the three-pane layout, live-preview Markdown, backlinks, a force-directed graph, 18 themes. Except it lives in your terminal, and it's built for the keyboard you already have your hands on.","Point it at a vault you already have. There's no import step, no database, no lock-in: it reads the same plain folder of Markdown files Obsidian does, and you can leave Obsidian open on that folder the whole time. Close this and your notes are exactly the files they were before.","It also comes with an AI assistant that works on your notes through the very same commands you do, so you can watch what it did instead of taking its word for it."],"features":["Notes. Live-preview Markdown with Obsidian's dialect: [[wikilinks]] (dimmed when they don't resolve yet), #tags, - [ ] tasks, > [!note] callouts, tables, and fenced code with syntax highlighting. Frontmatter is…","Editing. Long lines wrap, so nothing is ever cut off at the edge of the pane, and the arrow keys follow the rows you can see. Markdown is styled as you type it — headings coloured, bullets drawn as •, tasks as [☑],…","Pictures. ![[chart.png]] and are drawn in the reading pane — real pixels in Kitty, Ghostty, WezTerm, iTerm2 and anything that speaks sixel, and half-block mosaics everywhere else. Obsidian's |400 width works. Decoding…","Excalidraw. A .excalidraw.md note opens as the drawing, not as the wall of compressed base64 it is stored as. Shapes, arrows, freehand strokes and labels are drawn as vectors on a braille canvas, so a diagram reads the…","Explorer. The file tree opens with your most recently edited notes at the top, which is usually where you left off. s steps through the other orders: modified, created and file name, each in both directions. Folders…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/emeraldian/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6cb88fbdfc56a84d2b5b83291a7cfb163c988883ea758b6ad8205de3ec3bc2cb","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.877Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.877Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The best TUI for Obsidian. Your vault, the way you already know it: the three-pane layout, live-preview Markdown, backlinks, a force-directed graph, 18 themes. Except it lives in your terminal, and it's built for the keyboard you already have your hands on.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/emeraldian/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"The best TUI for Obsidian. Your vault, the way you already know it: the three-pane layout, live-preview Markdown, backlinks, a force-directed graph, 18 themes. Except it lives in your terminal, and it's built for the keyboard you already have your hands on.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/emeraldian/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6cb88fbdfc56a84d2b5b83291a7cfb163c988883ea758b6ad8205de3ec3bc2cb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/emeraldian/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:21.878Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-26T19:02:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iamrohithrnair/e